388 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 206 0 R
/E (Early and accurate grass monitoring is critical to maintaining healthy lawns. Uneven growth can affect appearance, density, and overall lawn quality. In densely planted gardens, overgrown patches often spread quickly )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
389 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 206 0 R
/T (1.2 Challenges in Traditional Lawn Maintenance)
/E (1.2 Challenges in Traditional Lawn Maintenance)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
390 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 206 0 R
/E (Traditional lawn mowing often cuts grass uniformly, without considering grass height or terrain variations. This leads to inefficient mowing, higher energy consumption, and uneven lawn appearance. Machines with fixed designs struggle to navigate narrow garden paths, sometimes damaging plants or missing overgrown areas entirely. Human-operated mowing is labor-intensive, inconsistent, and prone to errors, especially in large or uneven lawns, making it difficult to maintain optimal lawn maintenance.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
391 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 206 0 R
/T (1.1  Background of Automated Lawn Mowing)
/E (1.1  Background of Automated Lawn Mowing)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
392 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 206 0 R
/E (Lawn care has evolved far beyond traditional methods, with technology now playing a central role in improving efficiency while conserving energy. Automated lawn mowing leverages sensors, data analytics, and automation to make informed decisions, ensuring that operations such as grass cutting, navigation, and obstacle detection are handled efficiently. By monitoring grass and terrain in real time, robotic mowers can respond to conditions faster and optimize cutting patterns, reducing effort and environmental impact. This shift is especially significant for gardens and public lawns, which are maintained on large scales and are highly sensitive to surface variations)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
393 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 207 0 R
/E (imaking timely mowing essential. Smart detection enables targeted cutting, ensuring that only overgrown areas are trimmed, which saves energy, protects surrounding plants, and maintains healthy growth in well-maintained lawn sections.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
394 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 207 0 R
/E (Grass conditions vary across lawns, affecting growth patterns and surface appearance. Traditional mowing is slow, often involving manual effort and repeated trimming. Automated systems can measure grass height, terrain levels, and moisture in real time, providing insights into lawn conditions and maintenance needs. Integrating this data with navigation systems allows robotic mowers to make informed, timely movements, combining efficient grass cutting with smart lawn management for maximum efficiency.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
