/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 216 0 R
/E (A CNN-based classification model was developed using over 6,000 labeled grass images of lawns captured in garden and park conditions. Data were augmented with variations in lighting, angle, and scale. Feature extraction utilized visual texture combinations to detect height differences corresponding to overgrown grass. The trained model achieved 92.8 % accuracy in grass classification on validation data. The model runs locally on the Raspberry Pi using TensorFlow Lite, allowing offline inference and immediate mowing action without network dependency)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
