575 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 225 0 R
/E (Modern lawn maintenance requires efficient and sustainable solutions to manage grass growth, reduce manual effort, and improve lawn quality. The AUTO-MOW intelligent lawn mowing system was developed to address these challenges by integrating automation, sensing technologies, and data-driven decision making into a single lawn care platform. The system combines vision-based imaging, machine learning, terrain sensors, and LiDAR-based mapping to monitor lawn conditions and detect uneven grass growth at an early stage. The project demonstrates the design of a compact robotic system capable of navigating narrow garden paths while performing precise grass cutting. The adaptive drive mechanism enables the system to operate without damaging surrounding plants, while the integrated sensing modules collect real-time data on grass height and surface conditions. Based on this information, the system adjusts and performs the appropriate cutting action in precise levels, reducing energy wastage and improving mowing efficiency. By combining grass detection, terrain monitoring, and automated mowing within a single platform, AUTO-MOW supports the goals of smart landscaping and sustainable lawn care. The project highlights the potential of integrating robotics, artificial intelligence, and sensor technologies to create practical solutions that enhance lawn maintenance, optimize resource usage, and contribute to the future of intelligent outdoor automation.)
/Pg 36 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
